# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw capture data.  NEVER commit these.
#
# A single 60 s two-antenna capture is ~500 MB under sc8 and ~2 GB under fc32;
# the Winona_Visit tree alone is 24 GB.  GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB,
# and a blob that reaches a commit stays in history even after you delete it.
#
# Patterns are written WITHOUT a directory prefix so they match at any depth --
# `GNU_RADIO/*.npz` in the CHART repo silently failed to cover
# `GNU_RADIO/Winona_Visit/*.npz`, which is how the sidecars showed up untracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.iq
*.npz
*.dat

# Capture session trees
Winona_Visit/
keep/
day_one/
day_two/
day_three/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated plots.  Regenerate from the notebooks; committing them means every
# rerun shows as a binary diff.  Add a specific figure with `git add -f` if it
# needs to ship with the README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
